                        "entry_id": "d4d2f4ba-738a-3acc-a50f-00c07a2afd01",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Compensation for damage or loss; amends."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c8d164ac-ddbd-325e-a67d-71868ff98a9d",
                        "entry_id": "d4d2f4ba-738a-3acc-a50f-00c07a2afd01",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Retaliation or reprisal; vengeance."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d634bee2-f088-3e64-a0f9-6a93e9ca35e0",
                        "entry_id": "d4d2f4ba-738a-3acc-a50f-00c07a2afd01",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Return in kind; recompense, repayment, reward."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f8f19c82-0efb-4cde-aebe-e1aad04085c1",
                                "sense_id": "d634bee2-f088-3e64-a0f9-6a93e9ca35e0",
                                "text": "O, take his mother's thanks, a widow's thanks, / Till your strong hand shall help to give him strength / To make a more requital to your love."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ff1b9dae-d373-470d-9a9d-da43b747cfb8",
                                "sense_id": "d634bee2-f088-3e64-a0f9-6a93e9ca35e0",
                                "text": "My lord mayor, you have sundry times / Feasted myself and many courtiers more: / Seldom or never can we be so kind / To make requital of your courtesy."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2442ad71-a099-41d3-bd88-2c5de226f71f",
                                "sense_id": "d634bee2-f088-3e64-a0f9-6a93e9ca35e0",
                                "text": "In requittal [sic] of those well-intended offices, which you are pleased so emphatically to acknowledge, let me beg that you make in your devotions one petition for my eternal welfare."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "40df3ad6-3721-44a0-a28d-e0bf6f2fae0d",
                                "sense_id": "d634bee2-f088-3e64-a0f9-6a93e9ca35e0",
                                "text": "What is the requital that the Athenians of the earth give to those who have struggled through the stormy water, and the dark night, for their applause?—both reproach and scorn."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d96001a7-e849-4e62-8768-ff5cd6fa6553",
                                "sense_id": "d634bee2-f088-3e64-a0f9-6a93e9ca35e0",
                                "text": "But we are thinking here above all of the happiness that comes with the requital of love, of the case in which my love is returned with an equal love."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
